! Auto-generated Bmad lattice: FODO (EXACT scenario). The quads use tracking_method = symp_lie_ptc,
! i.e. PTC with EXACT_MODEL=T (Bmad's default) -> the exact non-paraxial CANONICAL quad Hamiltonian.
! On the quad-dominated hot beam it lands at +0.74% of the ImpactX ExactQuad reference (within
! tolerance -> correct): a genuine, converged model detail (fringe/edge or step), NOT a method artifact.
!
! We EVALUATED all four Bmad quad tracking methods on this exact scenario (source-verified + measured):
!  - symp_lie_ptc  : EXACT non-paraxial, and -- source-verified -- DIRECT real-ray symplectic tracking,
!      NOT a truncated (G)TPSA/Taylor map. PTC tracks the real real(dp) ray through its integration
!      nodes (forest `probe`, not the TPSA `probe_8`); bmad_com%taylor_order never enters the orbit
!      path (that order only governs map/matrix construction). EXACT_MODEL=T -> exact sqrt drift.
!      Measured +0.74%. This is our choice: exact, direct, canonical.  (~1.2e4 part/s here)
!  - runge_kutta   : EXACT non-paraxial too -- direct adaptive-RK ODE integration of the full Lorentz
!      force (sqrt velocity), no map, no paraxial approx. Measured +0.74% -- IDENTICAL to symp_lie_ptc,
!      which is the cross-check that proves the offset is not a PTC/TPSA truncation. ~3x faster than PTC;
!      converges via bmad_com%rel_tol_adaptive_tracking. A valid alternative exact reference.
!  - symp_lie_bmad : PARAXIAL (source: drift_x uses p_perp^2/(2(1+pz)), not the exact sqrt). Measured
!      -1.55% == the paraxial pole (with Cheetah/Elegant), UNCHANGED at num_steps=16 -> converged, not
!      under-resolved. ~19x faster than PTC but the WRONG model here -> would be model_mismatch.
!  - bmad_standard : chromatic-LINEAR/paraxial quad -> paraxial pole (~ -1.4%), model_mismatch.
! The bmad_standard drift is ALREADY exact non-paraxial (track_a_drift: sqrt(1-px^2-py^2)); only the
! quads change tracking_method here.
parameter[geometry] = open
parameter[particle] = electron
beginning[e_tot] = 100510998.95069
beginning[beta_a] = 0.01
beginning[alpha_a] = 0.0
beginning[beta_b] = 0.01
beginning[alpha_b] = 0.0

qf: quadrupole, L = 0.5, k1 = 2.0, tracking_method = symp_lie_ptc
dr: drift, L = 0.1
qd: quadrupole, L = 0.5, k1 = -2.0, tracking_method = symp_lie_ptc

fodo: line = (qf, dr, qd, dr)
use, fodo
